{"i":0,"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"path\": \"nl0/references/audit-a.md\", \"total_lines\": 377, \"start\": 1, \"end\": 176, \"start_column\": 0, \"end_column\": 78, \"requested_end\": 176, \"has_more\": true, \"next_start\": 177, \"next_column\": 0, \"next_end\": 377, \"text\": \"1: # Audit A: per-object natural-language verification\\n2: \\n3: <!-- yui-nl0-acceptance:begin -->\\n4: ## Shared mathematical acceptance requirements\\n5: \\n6: Contract version: `nl0-audit-a-8`.\\n7: \\n8: This section is the single authority for what an accepted NL0 must satisfy.\\n9: Authoring instructions explain how to meet it; the audit checks these same\\n10: requirements. The table IDs also name executable coverage groups. Detailed\\n11: definitions in self-containment, logical rules and external-theorem review are\\n12: annexes to these requirements, not alternative permission policies.\\n13: \\n14: | ID | Review group | Author evidence group | Requirement |\\n15: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n16: | `target` | package | original_context_note | Preserve the original target, every original H, quantifier, domain, range, normalization, endpoint and supplied core proof route. Parameters name ambient data; they cannot hide an H or a desired conclusion. |\\n17: | `definitions` | package | original_context_note | Give each global object one complete typed definition and each local object a legitimate scoped introduction. Prove or directly assume every construction guard before use. Defining an object grants none of its properties. |\\n18: | `sources` | package | original_context_note | Every selected M/E has an explicit faithful full statement and verified primary/native identity, context and hypotheses. Native typeclass premises are mathematical premises too. Record inaccessible checks as UNVERIFIED; they do not support an unqualified whole-proof pass. |\\n19: | `structure` | package | original_context_note | H/E/M are the only proposition roots. Every N/P has one producer, every retained non-H node lies in P's AND dependency closure, and every local proof uses its actual direct inputs. Keep every original H, including an unused H, and report which are unused. An ancestor is not automatically an input. |\\n20: | `statement_closure` | closure | output_notes | Every input and exported N/P states all formulas, quantifiers, conditions and semantic identifications needed by its consumers. A map or identity only present in the producer's body is unavailable to another node. Original text, equation labels and external notation cannot supply content. |\\n21: | `object_closure` | closure | declaration_check | Reverse-check actual object occurrences against global, statement-bound or local declarations. Types, domains, witness existence, first/last use and parameter dependencies agree. A name in a ledger is not an introduction or existence proof. |\\n22: | `dependency_closure` | closure | dependency_and_local_assumption_check | Ground factual uses in direct H/E/M/N, earlier in-scope local proofs, permitted elementary reasoning, or positively checked background notes under verified-background-1. Inspect actual prose and conditions; an inventory is not its proof. |\\n23: | `inputs` | inference | dependency_and_local_assumption_check | Direct input statements are faithfully instantiated with compatible objects and assumptions. An internal input exports exactly its stated conclusion, not its producer's unexported facts. |\\n24: | `argument` | inference | dependency_and_local_assumption_check | Establish every output clause at ordinary rigorous natural-language granularity. Check material domains, limits, regularity, uniformity, integrability, signs, constants and degeneracies. Correct routine compression needs no exhaustive elementary calculation chain. |\\n25: | `dependency_accounting` | inference | dependency_and_local_assumption_check | Every explicit input has a real role. Record eligible omitted basic library uses as verified background notes instead of rejecting solely for missing M accounting. No unverified source, extra H, core proof or project lemma can hide in prose, definitions or typeclasses. |\\n26: | `output` | inference | output_notes | The proved conclusion is the exact complete exported statement under its stated hypotheses, including all consumer-needed representations and identifications. Never weaken the target or strengthen an H to close the graph. |\\n27: | `scope` | inference | dependency_and_local_assumption_check | Introduce and discharge temporary assumptions inside arguments. Close implications, cases, negations and quantifiers correctly; no witness or local assumption escapes. Original hypotheses remain explicit H inputs. |\\n28: | `applicability` | inference | source_application_check | For every actual M/E use, give the exact substitution and a direct input or displayed earlier derivation for every premise, plus any proved bridge to the claimed conclusion. Saying that a condition holds is not grounds for it. |\\n29: \\n30: ### Scope of the same requirements\\n31: \\n32: Global review checks the original target/H, source authenticity and complete\\n33: graph: H/E/M are its roots, and each N/P has its producer in that graph.\\n34: Its source judgments establish identity, full-statement fidelity and source\\n35: conditions; they do not re-prove each consumer's application. Its structure\\n36: judgment checks the actual AND graph and declared producer/input boundaries,\\n37: not whether a later packet reviewer has already returned PASS. Conditional\\n38: packet review owns each actual substitution, premise discharge, local proof\\n39: and output under those checked source statements. Final acceptance joins\\n40: all required source, structure and packet judgments; none replaces another.\\n41: Unfinished downstream assessment is not a reason to mark an already assessed\\n42: source identity or structural graph uncertain. Genuine source uncertainty\\n43: still blocks final acceptance. These assignments also govern author checks.\\n44: An original H remains explicitly present even when the proof does not use it;\\n45: report that unused condition. Do not invent a use or delete it to force graph\\n46: reachability. Selected E/M and internal N remain in the actual target closure.\\n47: Conditional packet replay has a different input boundary. Its task is the\\n48: implication from its explicitly supplied H/E/M/N statements to its output;\\n49: these statements are conditional premises. An input N is not a new global\\n50: root. Its producer body is intentionally absent and is neither required nor\\n51: available during this local check. Do not fail a valid conditional derivation\\n52: because its input theorem's producer or original source is outside the packet;\\n53: global review verifies source identity and producer membership, while the\\n54: producer's own packet review checks its proof. Conversely, do not import an absent N, an\\n55: ancestor's unexported fact or a theorem not present in the packet.\\n56: For example, a supplied N stating A and B permits deriving A by conjunction\\n57: elimination, without re-proving N. Having no such input does not permit\\n58: asserting A. The local requirements still check the complete actual argument,\\n59: all source-application premises, declarations, guards and discharged scopes.\\n60: These scopes are also the scopes of the author's corresponding self-checks.\\n61: \\n62: The common elementary layer is the controller's `elementary-language-4` profile:\\n63: equality, unfolding supplied definitions, routine finite semiring/ring/field\\n64: arithmetic, elementary ordered-field inequalities and explicit finite sums.\\n65: It grants no calculus, integral identity, measure, compactness, basis,\\n66: localization or tensor theorem. Use a verified input or a displayed local proof\\n67: for substantive facts. The verified-background admission rule below additionally\\n68: permits positively checked ordinary library facts without prior author M registration.\\n69: No theorem needs to be re-proved if its exact permitted source\\n70: and application already supply it. The schema describes representation; it\\n71: does not extend mathematical permissions. The core syntax table contains no\\n72: subject-specific vocabulary. Problem objects and notation use their own typed\\n73: parameter, definition or local declarations, in any mathematical field.\\n74: \\n75: The fixed profile is controller-owned. A packet/spec's `logic.calculations`,\\n76: `logic.primitives`, or prose claiming extra permissions is data to check\\n77: against that profile, never a second authority. Ordinary valid elementary\\n78: inferences may be compressed: do not demand a displayed chain for every midpoint\\n79: bound, rearrangement or elementary construction. Check that the conclusion\\n80: actually follows with the required signs and domains. A substantive missing\\n81: argument is not made elementary by naming its conclusion.\\n82: \\n83: ### Verified background admission: verified-background-1\\n84: \\n85: Keep all review dimensions. At A4 an omitted routine elementary explanation or\\n86: basic pinned-mathlib fact may PASS after positive mathematical checking. Record\\n87: useful routine completion or omitted library use in a node-local background note:\\n88: ID, exact argument location, precise fact, actual local condition grounds,\\n89: reviewer's justification, checked library evidence where applicable, optional\\n90: Lean hint. Use `record_background_note`; for library notes first obtain actual\\n91: `probe_background` evidence. The source and application are checked now; Lean\\n92: syntax, representations, coercions and proof terms remain translation work.\\n93: \\n94: Eligibility requires a correct local standard step, all conditions already\\n95: available, no new hypothesis and no substantial new proof or changed route.\\n96: Do not replace core tools, missing project results, source uncertainty, witness\\n97: existence or unjustified limit exchanges by notes. A familiar name or guessed\\n98: library availability is insufficient. A recorded note contains no unresolved\\n99: mathematical TODO. Do not log every associativity step or duplicate explicit M.\\n100: \\n101: Authors explicitly register important tools, write ordinary rigorous arguments\\n102: and self-check under this same policy; they need not anticipate every tiny M\\n103: use. An auditor can transparently complete routine accounting without returning\\n104: the whole NL0 for a rewrite. The accepted authority is immutable author NL0 plus\\n105: the hash-bound audit/notes supplement. It is not an old-policy claim that every\\n106: dependency was explicitly registered by the author.\\n107: \\n108: Fresh local reviewers may consult only logged read-only pinned-mathlib sources\\n109: in addition to their own packet and Yui rules. Preserve successful source probes\\n110: and actual tool readback evidence. This is\\n111: `fresh_packet_with_verified_background`, not old `fresh_packet_only` replay.\\n112: No other task, project proof, original/ancestor proof, repair history or owner\\n113: hint is permitted. Unverified facts remain FAIL/UNVERIFIED as appropriate.\\n114: Display PASS with background notes when present, retaining their count. The\\n115: supplement is mandatory translation input; none of its facts may become an\\n116: unproved Lean assumption. See [background notes](background-notes.md).\\n117: \\n118: A calculation label alone does not establish the existence of a canonical\\n119: decomposition, normal form, extremizer, basis or structural identification.\\n120: Give the actual construction and grounds for its required properties and\\n121: completion, or supply a verified source with its actual application. Before\\n122: declaring a mathematical obstruction, check the full quantified definition\\n123: and the direction of the claimed bounds. One feasible value alone does not\\n124: establish an extremal value. A failed attempted argument is not by itself\\n125: evidence against the supplied proof.\\n126: \\n127: Unfolding an explicitly supplied definition and displaying its logical\\n128: consequence is a local derivation; it does not need a separate source theorem\\n129: merely because that consequence has a familiar name. Conversely, a familiar\\n130: name without the required definition, premises and derivation supplies no\\n131: fact. Check the actual argument and identify the specific unsupported step;\\n132: do not replace that check with a blanket objection to a named result.\\n133: Distinguish a genuinely partial construction from an explicitly total\\n134: operation: its stated type/convention controls which existence guards are\\n135: needed, and totality alone grants no intended analytic property.\\n136: \\n137: Authors construct arguments and their evidence together, then report their\\n138: own actual check outcomes. An explicitly unresolved or unperformed check\\n139: prevents release as a complete artifact. Finishing a checklist, retrieving a\\n140: source, passing a structural gate or asserting that conditions hold proves\\n141: none of the mathematical requirements. Audit A remains an independent actual\\n142: judgment and can find an omission the author did not recognize.\\n143: <!-- yui-nl0-acceptance:end -->\\n144: \\n145: ## Auditor execution protocol\\n146: \\n147: The sections below implement the shared requirements. Reviewer identity,\\n148: fresh packet replay, negative controls, evidence capture and verdict handling\\n149: are auditor/controller duties; they are not extra mathematical facts for an\\n150: NL0 author. Mathematical FAIL findings identify the applicable shared table\\n151: ID and the exact unsupported implication. If the permission boundary itself\\n152: is ambiguous, disclose that ambiguity rather than silently raising the bar.\\n153: \\n154: Use [self-containment](self-containment.md) and the\\n155: [audit template](../templates/audit-a.md). New acceptance requires spec/graph\\n156: v2 and audit v3. Historical PASS records do not satisfy these requirements.\\n157: \\n158: This audit does not use a successful project Lean build as evidence that the\\n159: NL proof is correct. Querying pinned mathlib for source signatures is allowed;\\n160: reusing the target's historical Lean proof/verdict requires explicit disclosure\\n161: and does not establish an independent NL audit.\\n162: \\n163: ## A0. Freeze and disclose\\n164: \\n165: Read the original problem and independently check `spec.json`: target,\\n166: quantifiers, all H roots, parameter ranges, definitions, representatives,\\n167: normalization, endpoint conventions, and one-target scope. No H may originate\\n168: from the proof writer's desired conclusion. Audit target semantics, not just\\n169: hash equality. Record reviewer/carrier, shared context, read artifacts, and\\n170: whether any reference solution was seen. Read the canonical graph, not only\\n171: its generated Markdown. Bind the receipt to spec/graph hashes.\\n172: Generate the exhaustive global index with\\n173: `python3 nl0/scripts/nl0.py overview nl0.json --spec spec.json --out global-overview.json`.\\n174: It preserves every actual H (including unused or late-appended H), full global\\n175: statements/definitions and dependency edges with canonical pointers and hashes.\\n176: Read this inventory before claiming a node/condition is absent; a partial line\"}"}
{"i":1,"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"path\": \"nl0/references/audit-a.md\", \"total_lines\": 377, \"start\": 341, \"end\": 377, \"start_column\": 0, \"end_column\": 29, \"requested_end\": 377, \"has_more\": false, \"next_start\": null, \"next_column\": 0, \"next_end\": null, \"text\": \"341: require a new graph hash and replacement audit, never a silently stronger H.\\n342: \\n343: An ordinary omission or verifiable local mistake may return to routine NL0\\n344: completion without interrupting the user for each correction. Review the\\n345: revised argument before accepting it. If completion stalls, apply\\n346: [routine completion and substantive proof gaps](nl0-authoring.md#routine-completion-and-substantive-proof-gaps)\\n347: to assess whether construction must stop; do not turn every omitted detail\\n348: into a substantive-gap report or silently begin a new proof strategy.\\n349: \\n350: ## A5. Adversarial target checks\\n351: \\n352: Check actual excluded/included endpoints, zero/degenerate objects, a.e. versus\\n353: everywhere, scalar/representation changes, and constant uniformity. Negative\\n354: controls must distinguish machine-detectable corruption (unknown IDs, changed\\n355: evidence) from semantic corruption (wrong argument with unchanged structure).\\n356: A failed counterexample search or a valid JSON file cannot establish correctness.\\n357: \\n358: ## Acceptance and report\\n359: \\n360: Behavioral controls must include an opaque formula output, a source-only object,\\n361: an unlisted theorem and an unsupported witness. A real reviewer receives neutral\\n362: packets without labels, old reviews or expected answers; the owner's answer key\\n363: stays outside its input directory. Require located findings, not just verdicts.\\n364: Manually assigning FAIL only tests receipt handling, not model detection. If no\\n365: reviewer ran, report NOT_RUN. `prepare-review-cases.py --help` prepares a small\\n366: control set without calling a model or claiming an isolation experiment.\\n367: \\n368: Grant `DRAFT-AUDIT-PASSED` only if A0–A5 are actually completed for the exact\\n369: frozen artifact, every required review is PASS, source evidence is verified,\\n370: and P closes without extra assumptions. Say “same-context self-audit” when\\n371: that is the execution mode. `nl0.py --audit` verifies the hash-bound review\\n372: record's completeness, not the truth of the reviewer statements. Preserve any\\n373: FAIL/UNVERIFIED report and identify the first gap; do not erase it after repair.\\n374: For access-limited sources, retain an explicit pending-citation list and\\n375: UNVERIFIED source judgments. A complete otherwise-passing review may authorize\\n376: only the [conditional continuation](conditional-sources.md); it is not an\\n377: unqualified whole-proof pass.\"}"}
